# SPA fallback.
#
# PINGO routes on the client with react-router: /chats, /settings/privacy and
# the rest exist only in JavaScript, not as files on disk. Cloudflare Pages
# serves static files, so without this rule a visitor who opens a link directly,
# refreshes a page, or is returned to /auth/google by the OAuth redirect gets a
# 404 -- even though the app itself is fine.
#
# 200, not 301: the URL must stay what the user asked for so the router can read
# it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to / and lose the route.
#
# Do not list Google Search Console verification paths here. Rewriting
# /foo.html ↔ /foo loops with Cloudflare's automatic HTML pretty-URLs.
/*  /index.html  200
